{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>There is an evil</b>. The word יוצא appears with its lamed as alef, like verbs with heh, like ואת מאמר מרדכי אסתר עושה, and it is feminine, for the masculine is יוצא, and like it is כעגלה דשא. And if it is with alef, it follows the pattern of words with heh, like דוה, therefore ספות הרוה, even though the grammarian said that the alef of דש״א is a substitution for heh. And the meaning of this verse is connected to the preceding one about authority, for the ruler, by his governance, requires us to do things contrary to truth, and it appears as though it is inadvertence and not knowledge."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase 'בעלי ה״א' refers to word classes whose characteristic letter is heh; the grammarian (הגאון בעל הדקדוק, likely referring to a different authority than Saadia) is cited on the alef-heh interchange in דש״א."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:53.349972866Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}